  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 213 AM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nA upper level low to the south will continue to track eastward \nas a upper level ridge builds in from the west with strong \nsoutherly winds keeping temperatures in the 50s. SFC winds will \nbe the strongest across northern Nebraska into north central \nNebraska Monday and Tuesday with winds around 15 to 20 mph and \ngust up to 35 mph. On Wednesday a cold front will move into the \narea, ahead of the front compressional heating will warm \ntemperatures into the upper 50s to low 60s across southwest \nNebraska into north central Nebraska, making Wednesday the \nwarmest day of the week. There will be a slight chance of \nscattered precipitation chances Wednesday afternoon and evening.\nTemperatures cool into the low 50s for Thursday. \n\nAttention then turns to a system moving in to end the week \nFriday and Saturday. As the upper level low moves onshore into \nthe western CONUS Friday and moves eastward increasing \nprecipitation chances Friday. Will need to continue to monitor \nthe system as models at this time are suggesting the system \ncould potentially move across the Central CONUS as a fairly \nstrong closed low system, however as this is still pretty far \nout in the forecast and the system is still well offshore, the \ntrack and strength could still change as we approach the end of \nnext week.",
